WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:05.240
Though Halloween is renowned among horror
hounds, the film is not without its flaws,

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.120
oddities, and strange leaps of logic.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:11.750
None of these examples can diminish the film's
overall legacy, but let's not pretend there

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:15.350
aren't some dumb things everyone ignores about
John Carpenter's Halloween.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:21.980
Major horror films of the 1970s, like Carrie
and Last House on the Left, tended to cast

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.360
20-somethings in the roles of teens.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:28.210
In this respect, Halloween is no different,
but that doesn't make the casting any less

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:28.720
distracting.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.220
With the exception of Jamie Lee Curtis, who
was 19 at the time Halloween was released,

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.300
the actors who played the teenagers were all
well into their twenties.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:41.440
P.J. Soles, the actress who plays Laurie's
cheerleader friend Lynda, was 28 years old.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:46.460
Similarly, Laurie's other friend Annie was
portrayed by 29-year-old Nancy Kyes.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:50.739
When all three girls are together on screen,
it's incredibly awkward to watch two grown

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.780
women pretend to be high school girls.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:56.540
When paired with Curtis, who is noticeably
younger than the other two actresses, the

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.459
glaring age differences are impossible to
ignore.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:00.879
"I forgot my chemistry book."

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:02.740
"So who cares?

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:05.820
I always forget my chemistry book, and my
math book, and my English book..."

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:11.360
After Michael breaks out of Smith's Grove
sanitarium at the beginning of the film, Dr.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:14.560
Loomis rightfully fears what Michael will
do with his newfound freedom.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:18.940
He takes his concerns to the police but is
promptly brushed off, leaving him to hunt

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:20.010
Michael on his own.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.920
"Well, he was your patient, Doctor, if precautions
weren't strong enough, you should've told

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:23.580
somebody."

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:24.380
"I told everybody!"

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.880
Suspecting Michael will return to his childhood
home, Loomis makes his way to Haddonfield.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:33.740
On his way, he stops at a payphone and by
pure circumstance, stumbles onto an abandoned

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:34.240
car.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:38.480
While the camera pans to show the audience
the driver's body lying nearby, Loomis is

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:39.740
not privy to the murder.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:44.760
Nevertheless, the good doctor somehow surmises
that the abandoned car and a stray matchbook

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:47.200
are solid proof that Michael Myers was there.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:52.280
What's so bizarre about this scene isn't just
the unlikely circumstances or Loomis' apparent

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:56.160
sixth sense, but the fact that he doesn't
appear to report the crime at all.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:00.640
If Loomis is genuinely concerned about what
he found, why wouldn't he call the police?

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:04.960
If he had taken even a minute to look around
and not run off after finding a random matchbook

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:08.909
on the ground, he would have seen the dead
body, and it would have likely forced the

00:02:08.909 --> 00:02:10.120
police to cooperate.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:14.459
While we don't know much about the specific
events that triggered Loomis' immense fear

00:02:14.459 --> 00:02:19.219
of Michael, it's safe to say the doctor knows
far more about the killer's violent tendencies

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:20.060
than anyone else.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:24.560
After breaking out of confinement, stealing
a car, assaulting a woman, and killing an

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.260
innocent man, you'd think anyone hunting Michael
would at least be cautious.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:31.560
Surprisingly, the hunt for Michael is incredibly
low-key.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:35.740
Loomis seeks out the help of Haddonfield's
sheriff, Leigh Brackett, and the two hunt

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:36.580
Michael alone.

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:41.760
At some point, the sheriff suggests a full-blown
man-hunt, but Loomis tosses the idea aside

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.180
for fear of causing a panic.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:46.940
"If you do that, they'll see him on every
street corner, they'll look for him in every

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:47.460
house.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:50.640
Just tell your men to keep their mouths shut
and their eyes open."

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:55.480
Meanwhile, Michael is walking around, killing
teenagers and terrorizing Laurie.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:59.940
It seems hypocritical from Loomis of all people
to prefer discretion over action.

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:04.620
At the beginning of the film, he was desperately
seeking police help, but when he finally gets

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.930
it, he turns the offer down.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:10.060
If a full search was organized, maybe Laurie's
friends wouldn't have been butchered.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.200
When Annie and Laurie stumble onto a recently
robbed hardware store, Annie's father tells

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.460
them that someone has stolen a Halloween mask,
some knives, and rope.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:22.840
The robbery must have just happened, as the
alarm is blaring in the background, and a

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:25.550
group of police officers are actively surveying
the scene.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:26.900
"What happened?"

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:30.380
"Oh, uh, somebody broke into the hardware
store, probably kids."

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:34.519
Given the context, the film is hinting that
Michael is the one who stole the mask and

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.360
the murder tools.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:39.559
In theory, that makes sense, but given the
fact that the girls had already encountered

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:44.400
a masked Michael far before the robbery supposedly
occurred, he couldn't have stolen the mask.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:48.720
The first time we see Michael after he escapes
from Smith's Grove is when he waits outside

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.660
of Laurie's school, clearly already wearing
the mask.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:56.240
Hours later, when Laurie walks home with her
friends, the group encounters Michael twice.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:04:00.420
And right before Laurie goes out with Annie,
she spots him again outside of her window.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:05.010
All of these occurrences happen before Michael
supposedly robs the store, and yet in all

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.480
of them, he's wearing the mask.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:11.199
Unless he robbed another store and took another
identical mask for good measure, this timeline

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.420
just doesn't add up.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:17.580
Though it's understandable that Laurie would
make some mistakes in a life or death situation,

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:20.720
it's less acceptable that she would make the
same mistake three times.

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:25.140
When Michael surprises Laurie from inside
the Doyle house, she reflexively stabs the

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:26.380
killer with a knitting needle.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:29.140
Michael falls to the ground, seemingly defeated.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:33.920
In typical horror fashion, however, he is
very much alive and pursues Laurie again shortly

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:34.420
after.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:38.480
Again, Laurie attacks Michael, jabbing him
in the eye with a coat hanger and stabbing

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:39.200
him with a knife.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:43.620
Michael is down once more, but instead of
checking to see if he's done for good, Laurie

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:46.760
makes the same mistake as before and just
assumes he's dead.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.820
Not ready to call it quits, Michael gets right
back up.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:53.880
This time, Loomis takes the offensive and
shoots him, causing Michael to fall off of

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:54.560
the balcony.

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:59.140
Despite Laurie failing to kill Michael twice
before, she and Loomis decide it's better

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:03.410
to have a conversation, rather than check
to make sure the fall or the gunshots successfully

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:04.260
killed Michael.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:05.580
"It was the boogeyman."

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:09.200
"As a matter of fact, it was."

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.720
By the time anyone bothers to look, he's long
gone.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:17.050
If Loomis or Laurie had cared enough to check
Michael's pulse, they wouldn't have to worry

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:19.140
about him continuing his killing spree.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.280
Then again, how else could we have had so
many Halloween sequels?

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:27.740
Being a low budget independent film created
in a short period, Halloween naturally couldn't

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:32.680
avoid its fair share of little mistakes, ranging
from continuity errors to production goofs

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.840
that eagle-eyed viewers may be able to catch.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:38.820
For example, a crew member is reflected in
the phone booth glass right before Loomis

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:42.040
discovers the driver Michael killed on his
way to Haddonfield.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:46.390
Though it can be a bit hard to notice, you
can see Lynda stumble as she and Bob head

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:48.250
upstairs in the Wallace house.

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:50.880
Apparently, P.J. Soles didn't just lose her
footing.

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:52.820
The actress tripped over a dolly track.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:57.150
And when Annie is teasing Laurie about Michael
in front of the hedges, a puff of smoke is

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:58.580
briefly caught on camera.

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:02.140
According to John Carpenter, the smoke came
from his own cigarette.

